// M5 token S5 (): mint/burn on the approved supply-as-a-ledger model (decision ,
// docs/process/SUPPLY_LEDGER_DECISION.md). Mint/burn are the one place a token creates or destroys
// circulating value; modeled as a bare credit/debit with no counterparty they would break
// `assert balanced`. The decision makes total supply an explicit `token.supply` ledger so mint and
// burn are ordinary BALANCED debit/credit pairs — feature-by-balanced-composition over the existing
// model, NOT a new primitive. This test proves, from ONE spec per operation: both legs post on the
// happy path and render to Solidity AND PostgreSQL; `assert balanced` stays intact on both rails;
// the security artifact surfaces the mint/burn authority + the supply-ledger audit surface; and an
// unauthorized or malformed supply_approved suppresses BOTH legs (fail-closed, no value moves) —
// the required invalid/unauthorized case.
//
// DEFINE: %{mint}  = %curated0-source
// DEFINE: %{mscen} = %curated0-scenario
// DEFINE: %{burn}  = %curated1-source
// DEFINE: %{bscen} = %curated1-scenario
//
// MINT happy path — both legs post (debit token.supply / credit token.balance).
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=test-realization --scenario=%{mscen} %{mint} -o %t.mr
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINTREAL < %t.mr/test-realization.json
// MINTREAL: "eventChain"
// MINTREAL: SupplyDebitDebited
// MINTREAL: HolderCreditCredited
//
// MINT renders to Solidity from that spec — a balanced pair on the supply + balance ledgers.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=solidity --scenario=%{mscen} %{mint} -o %t.msol
// RUN: cat %t.msol/src/*.sol | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINTSOL
// MINTSOL: net[_k]["token.supply"] -= int256(u_amount);
// MINTSOL: emit SupplyDebitDebited(u_supply_id, u_amount, u_currency);
// MINTSOL: net[_k]["token.balance"] += int256(u_amount);
// MINTSOL: emit HolderCreditCredited(u_holder_id, u_amount, u_currency);
// MINTSOL: require(debitTotal[_k] == creditTotal[_k], "not balanced");
//
// MINT renders to PostgreSQL from the SAME spec — the same balanced pair + the balance check.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=postgres --scenario=%{mscen} %{mint} -o %t.mpg
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINTPG < %t.mpg/procedure.sql
// MINTPG: VALUES ({{'[^']+'}}, 'supply_debit', 'token.supply', p_supply_id, p_amount, p_currency, -(p_amount), p_mint_id);
// MINTPG: VALUES ({{'[^']+'}}, 'holder_credit', 'token.balance', p_holder_id, p_amount, p_currency, p_amount, p_mint_id);
// MINTPG: RAISE EXCEPTION 'not balanced for %', p_mint_id;
//
// MINT security artifact surfaces the mint/burn authority + the supply-ledger audit surface.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=security --scenario=%{mscen} %{mint} -o %t.msec
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINTSEC < %t.msec/security.json
// MINTSEC: reserved supply ledger `token.supply`
// MINTSEC: created (mint: supply
// MINTSEC: authority-gated (see the guard above), so unauthorized supply change is suppressed fail-closed
// (The negative — an UNGUARDED `token.supply` leg must raise an advisory, never claim fail-closed —
// is the self-contained regression fixture token/unguarded_supply.neu.)
//
// BURN happy path — both legs post (debit token.balance / credit token.supply).
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=test-realization --scenario=%{bscen} %{burn} -o %t.br
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BURNREAL < %t.br/test-realization.json
// BURNREAL: HolderDebitDebited
// BURNREAL: SupplyCreditCredited
//
// BURN renders to BOTH backends from one spec, balanced intact.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=solidity --scenario=%{bscen} %{burn} -o %t.bsol
// RUN: cat %t.bsol/src/*.sol | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BURNSOL
// BURNSOL: net[_k]["token.balance"] -= int256(u_amount);
// BURNSOL: net[_k]["token.supply"] += int256(u_amount);
// BURNSOL: require(debitTotal[_k] == creditTotal[_k], "not balanced");
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=postgres --scenario=%{bscen} %{burn} -o %t.bpg
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BURNPG < %t.bpg/procedure.sql
// BURNPG: VALUES ({{'[^']+'}}, 'holder_debit', 'token.balance', p_holder_id, p_amount, p_currency, -(p_amount), p_burn_id);
// BURNPG: VALUES ({{'[^']+'}}, 'supply_credit', 'token.supply', p_supply_id, p_amount, p_currency, p_amount, p_burn_id);
//
// UNAUTHORIZED mint (supply_approved == 0) -> suppressed: NEITHER leg posts, no supply is created.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=test-realization --scenario=%S/mint_unauthorized.json %{mint} -o %t.mu
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MDENY < %t.mu/test-realization.json
// MDENY-NOT: SupplyDebitDebited
// MDENY-NOT: HolderCreditCredited
//
// MALFORMED mint (supply_approved == 2, out of range) -> suppressed fail-closed: only an exact 1
// posts, so any other value can never mint.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=test-realization --scenario=%S/mint_malformed.json %{mint} -o %t.mm
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MDENYM < %t.mm/test-realization.json
// MDENYM-NOT: SupplyDebitDebited
// MDENYM-NOT: HolderCreditCredited
//
// UNAUTHORIZED burn (supply_approved == 0) -> suppressed: NEITHER leg posts, no supply is destroyed.
// RUN: %neutrino-gen --target=test-realization --scenario=%S/burn_unauthorized.json %{burn} -o %t.bu
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BDENY < %t.bu/test-realization.json
// BDENY-NOT: HolderDebitDebited
// BDENY-NOT: SupplyCreditCredited
